-- title:
--   Totally ramified q-cyclotomic extension of a DVR with 𝔪=(q)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 3$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_{A_0} = (q)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain that is an $A_0$-algebra such that the structure map $A_0 \to A$ is injective and $A$ is finite as an $A_0$-module. Let $\zeta \in A$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity (in the sense that $\zeta^q = 1$ and $\zeta$ is not a root of $X^n - 1$ for $0 < n < q$), and assume $A_0[\zeta] = A$, that is, the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\zeta$ is everything. Let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. The conclusion is a conjunction of three assertions. First, a universal property of $\zeta$: for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $S$ and every $z \in S$ with $\sum_{i < q} z^i = 0$, there is an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $f : A \to S$ with $f(\zeta) = z$. Second, $\varpi = u(1-\zeta)$ for some unit $u$ of $A$, so $1 - \zeta$ is a uniformiser. Third, $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon q$ in $A$ for some unit $\varepsilon$ of $A$, so $A/A_0$ is totally ramified of degree $q-1$.
--
--   This records the standard structure of the $q$-th cyclotomic extension of an absolutely unramified discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $q$: $A \cong A_0[X]/(\Phi_q)$ (expressed through the universal property in the first clause), $1-\zeta$ is a uniformiser, and $q$ is a unit times the $(q-1)$-st power of the uniformiser. It is used in the construction of the local cyclotomic rings appearing in the deformation-theoretic part of the argument, being cited by [`IsPrimitiveRoot.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top`](thm.html#IsPrimitiveRoot.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top).
